## Summary of the methods

**`groupSerializableRollbackRequestsBasedOnFileGroup`** — A thin wrapper that delegates to the generic grouping method, passing in `SerializableHoodieRollbackRequest`-specific accessor functions (constructor, partition path, file ID, latest base instant, log blocks to delete, files to delete).

**`groupRollbackRequestsBasedOnFileGroup`** (generic version) — Takes a list of rollback requests plus accessor functions. Per the doc comment, its goal is that each file group ends up with at most two non-empty rollback requests: one for the base file, one for all log files to be rolled back.

Its logic:
1. Builds a map keyed by a `Pair` of partition path and file ID, grouping requests per file group (null partition paths default to `""`).
2. For each group, it iterates the requests. Requests with non-empty log blocks have their log blocks merged into a single map; if such a request also unexpectedly has files to delete, it logs a warning (`"Only one of the following should be non-empty..."`) and emits a separate request for those files.
3. Requests without log blocks are passed through unchanged.
4. If any log blocks were collected, a new consolidated request for all log files in that file group is created.
5. Results are flattened and collected into a list.

If you want the exact source, it's available under the Apache License 2.0 in the Apache Hudi repository (`RollbackUtils.java`), which you can retrieve directly.

